{{Stealnotes
| name = Amphibian Rhapsody
| desc = {{H|Rubick}}'s basic abilities' {{M|cooldown}} utilize the custom [[HUD]] element upon acquiring Amphibian Rhapsody.
}}

 {{#lst:Largo/Calculations|ultimate}}

* Applies the following ability effects on self upon cast:
** Switches Largos <span class="fas fa-square" style=“font-size:15px”></span> <span class="fas fa-square" style=“font-size:15px”></span> <span class="fas fa-square" style=“font-size:15px”></span> <span class="far fa-square" style=“font-size:15px”></span> first, second, and third ability slot to {{A|Largo|Bullbelly Blitz}}, {{A|Largo|Hotfeet Hustle}}, and {{A|Largo|Island Elixir}} respectively.
** The [[toggle]] component has the following properties:
*** Not affected by {{M|silence}} sources.
*** Does not interrupt Largo's {{M|channeling}} abilities.
*** Does not self-{{M|disarm}}.
*** Does not break Largo's current {{M|invisibility}} sources.

* The 1st proc interval does not need to be on time.

* The {{A|Largo|Amphibian Rhapsody}}-based ability effects are applied as follows upon the 2nd proc interval:
** {{Symbol|Dot|Off}} {{Symbol|Dot|On}} {{Symbol|Dot|Off}} ...
*** {{Symbol|Affect|Self}}
**** {{M|Disarm}}
**** {{Symbol|Modifier|Stack}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Code|largo_amphibian_rhapsody_self}}
****** Grants self 1 ({{Symbol|bonus agh}} {{ValueColor||2|agh}}) stack per hit interval.
****** Reduces the stack by 1 per missed interval.
*** {{Symbol|Affect|Ally}}
***# Applies the respective ability effects within the radius.
***# {{Symbol|bonus t3l}} {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Code|largo_amphibian_rhapsody_ambient_buff}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Aura}}
***#* {{cf|talnotes}}
***#** This ability component considers {{M|clones}}, {{M|illusions}}, and {{M|creep-heroes}} as heroes.

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Amphibian Rhapsody icon0}}
| desc = Largo gets ready to groove. He is disarmed and his ability bar switches to 3 song abilities, each with different effects. Songs are only effective if strummed on the beat.<br><br>Every time he strums successfully, he gains a stack of Groovin'. Each stack gives him bonus armor and reduces the mana cost of every song, but he loses a stack if he misses a beat. Stacks linger for a short duration when Largo's song ends.
}}

